Part 1. Third-party material contained in this repository
========================================================================

1.1  Ibex RISC-V core (source files, unmodified)

     Location:   designs/src/aichip_sv/ibex/
                 23 files: 21 SystemVerilog sources, 1 Verilog source and
                 1 SystemVerilog header.
     Origin:     https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex
                 The files are taken, without change, from the copy that
                 ships with OpenROAD-flow-scripts under
                 flow/designs/src/ibex_sv/. OpenROAD-flow-scripts records
                 that copy as cloned from lowRISC/ibex at commit
                 77d801001554cce8fe69e742e96539eecbe74425 and pruned to
                 the source files in use.
     License:    Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)
     Copyright notices, as they appear in the file headers:
                 Copyright lowRISC contributors.
                 Copyright 2018 ETH Zurich and University of Bologna,
                 see also CREDITS.md.
                 Copyright 2017 ETH Zurich and University of Bologna,
                 see also CREDITS.md.

     Sixteen of the files carry an ETH Zurich and University of Bologna
     notice next to the lowRISC one (2017 in ibex_pkg.sv, 2018 in the other
     fifteen). Six carry the lowRISC notice only. One, ibex_counter.sv, has
     no header in the upstream copy and is covered by the same upstream
     license. The CREDITS.md file that the headers mention is part of the
     Ibex repository and is not reproduced here.

     The neighbouring directory designs/src/aichip_sv/IBEX_SRAM/ is
     ScaleNative code. It is not part of Ibex, despite the name.

     Two ScaleNative files, rtl/IBEX_SRAM/pe_ibex_wrapper.sv and
     rtl/IBEX_SRAM/pe_top.sv (and their copies under
     designs/src/aichip_sv/IBEX_SRAM/), repeat parameter and port
     declarations of ibex_core.sv, as is needed to instantiate the core.
     Those declarations originate from Ibex and are covered by the same
     Apache License, Version 2.0.

1.2  Files derived from OpenROAD-flow-scripts

     Origin:     https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts
     License:    BSD 3-Clause License (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt, first text)
     Copyright:  Copyright (c) 2018-2023, The Regents of the University of California
                 All rights reserved.
     Changes:    Copyright (c) 2026, The ScaleNative Authors, under the same
                 BSD 3-Clause terms.

     (a) patches/orfs-local.patch
         A patch against flow scripts under flow/scripts/. It reproduces
         unchanged upstream lines as context around the added lines.

     (b) designs/asap7/aichip_vector/constraint.sdc
         designs/asap7/m1_vector_1670.sdc
         Timing constraints adapted from the example constraint file that
         ships with the upstream Ibex design (flow/designs/asap7/ibex/
         constraint.sdc). They differ from it in the clock period, in
         leaving out the two clock-latency lines, and in the comments.

     (c) designs/asap7/aichip_pe_top/constraint.sdc
         designs/asap7/aichip_tensor_signoff/constraint.sdc
         designs/asap7/m1_tensor_1670.sdc
         Timing constraints that open with the clock-definition lines used
         by the upstream example constraint files. The rest of each file
         was written for this project.

     (d) designs/asap7/aichip_pe_top/config.mk
         designs/asap7/aichip_vector/config.mk
         designs/asap7/aichip_tensor_signoff/config.mk
         Design configuration files laid out after the example config.mk
         files that ship with OpenROAD-flow-scripts. Individual variable
         settings coincide with those examples. The remaining content was
         written for this project.

